# Keep the build context (and the SSH transfer for remote Unraid builds) small.
# The Dockerfile installs deps fresh (npm ci) and builds Next.js itself, so none
# of the local build artifacts below are needed — and shipping them is slow.

# Dependencies (reinstalled via npm ci inside the image)
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build outputs (rebuilt inside the image)
**/.next
**/dist
backend/dist
frontend/.next

# VCS / editor / CI
.git
.gitignore
.github
.vscode

# Secrets and local env (compose reads .env locally; never bake into the image)
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Local data / caches / logs
data
appdata
**/*.log
**/.cache
**/coverage
**/.turbo

# Docs and planning (not needed at build time)
*.md
docs
plans
plan*.md
DEVELOPMENT_HISTORY.md
assets
examples

# OS cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
